# Voice & copy guide

Free-form brand voice. Skills read this verbatim and use it to constrain copy
generation and review. Keep it short and concrete — bullets beat paragraphs.

## Tone

- Direct, warm, never corporate.
- Speak to one person, not "users" or "customers".
- Active voice. Short sentences.

## Vocabulary

**Use:** signal, ship, real, simple
**Avoid:** synergy, unlock, leverage (verb), revolutionary, game-changing

## Do

- Lead with the user's problem.
- Be specific: numbers, names, and concrete examples.
- End with one clear action (the CTA).

## Don't

- Don't promise outcomes we can't measure.
- Don't open with the brand name.
- Don't use emojis in headlines (primary_text OK, sparingly).

## Example copy

> **Primary text:** Trying to keep your weekday planning under 10 minutes? Here's the workflow we use.
>
> **Headline:** Plan your day in 10 minutes
>
> **Description:** Free template. No sign-up to view.

## Banned claims

- Anything implying medical, financial, or legal outcomes.
- Comparative claims against named competitors.
